/-
Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/K12/Sim2/ListU.lean: CONDITIONAL.

Can the hypotheses be met together at a real run? NOT KNOWN. Object by object. h: the head has
members at each of the goals' two named sets of public files (`headMember_named`,
AtFullSide/Top/HeadMemberAtGap.lean). hb: under the head the plan's sub-protocols of the kind K14
are made (`blocks_head`, NearAtHead.lean: a list); that they are eight is the text of `blocks`. hAr:
that the maker returns at the wide filling: a premise here. G with hP: a term lies at this G's own
type: `theGAtBase` with `theGAtBase_prover` (E2E/TheG.lean; not imported): its
prover at the return's prover is the return's; BUT its two arguments, the threads' parts and the
kinds' rows, have no known value. The list L, a value T of `ThreadsP`, ready's and runC's return,
and that the second part is called at any coin: NO TERM AND NO LAW KNOWN TO US: A CONDITIONAL WITH
NO KNOWN MEMBER. Where the part is never called the ends hold for nothing: the rule's own limit.
hleft, THE ONE CLAUSE ON VALUES, is paid by nothing here.

What is here. `OnAtRun₂` (Honest/Law/OwedAtRun.lean: the condition On of one list of the shared
chain, at a run that has returned, before a part that the run has called) at the list of the
proximity test on G_u of the proof file's shared chain (piece 9). The list is bound by four
equations (`IsListAtU`): its place; its parts with their simulators, `testPairs` of the job and the
simulators' job; its On, the library's `onFreeT` (Sim/TreesExact.lean); its bud, `budOpened`: the On
and the bud at which `good_testOnU` (Sim2/SlotU.lean) has `Good`. The fellow of
Sim2/ListAtHead.lean's `onAtRun_head` at the first chain's last test, and of `onAtRun_folded` at the
key file.

  `LeftAtStandU`   what is left at one stand: one field, rowsSay : `SaysAt` (AsksWhole.lean).
  `IsListAtU`   the four equations on the list.
  `LeftAtEveryStandU`   `LeftAtStandU` at every stand of one run, under all that the rule holds
      there.
  `first_ties_at_shared_test`, `seat_at_U`   the seat: what `onFreeT_head_U` asks on the place, the
      cut and the challenges.
  `onAtRun_U`   the statement at a free prover `G.prover H`, at the job `jobHeadU` at that prover's
      own stored columns and at any two readers of the index and of the table's randomness.
  `leftAtStandU_where_the_fold_fails`   at the fall-back `LeftAtStandU` holds for nothing.
  `jobRealU_at_head`   the job that `halfU` lays is the head's job, as a `ManyJob`.
  `onAtRun_U_at_return`   the statement where that prover is the one that the maker returns at the
      wide filling, at the job that `halfU` lays there (`jobRealU`).

THE ENDS ARE `OnAtRun₂` ITSELF: there the carried blocks ca are bound by carriedAt Bk k 1 … = .ok ca
at the run's own coins k, and the stand m by the walk's own equation. No ∃ of this file's own stands
in an end. hleft is asked at EVERY m and ca, under ALL the rule's hypotheses at the second member,
the front's equation among them, and that the member stands there (`StandsAt`). What `InsideOf`
hands is the invariant at the border in front of the test and a play from there, not a sentence at m
itself.

THE PREMISES, SORTED. PUBLIC (facts on the public files): h · hb. THE MAKER (at the return alone):
hAr: `onlineProverFromPublicFiles` returns at `onlineProverPartsInUse I secondHashFunction S' O`, with its letters I, S', O. These files
call it "the wide filling" throughout; others' names for it: the base, the unread
filling. THE FILLING. At W₀ := the matrices, I := `matrixInput`, S' := Sz.ref, O := openHonest,
`onlineProverPartsInUse I secondHashFunction S' O` is `baseFilling` by its text (E2E/BaseMaker.lean). Two things
are not shown here or beneath: that the own test's rows are ready, and that the lent o_sp words
are tied at the tests on G_u and on G_omega through `OnlineProverParts.through`. The wide filling is defined
in Honest/K1/Law/WSideAtFill.lean. This file does not show that the maker returns at it:
hAr is a premise here; `maker_returns_base`
(AtFullSide/K1/MakerReturnsBase.lean) is not called.
THE RUN: T (`ThreadsP`: the rule's own letter) · hρ (the challenges have the declared form)
· hR · hrun. WHICH OBJECTS: hA · hJs (the two jobs) · hL (the list: `IsListAtU`). The list's fields
A and B stay free: `OnAtRun₂` reads neither, nor bud. bud₂ at this list (`BudDebts`) is not this
file's: a payer lies, `budOwed₂_at_U` (Johnson/M1/BudU.lean; not called); nor is
what the two senders in front owe toward it. ON THE FILLING (which halves the search finds in the
prover's shared list): hg (the test's) · hgU · hgO (the two sendings'). At the return they are not
asked; their payers are `shared_test_found_of_laid` (Sim2/FoundOwnAndShared.lean) and
`sendings_found` (Sim2/TreesSharedTest.lean). hP (at the return): the rule's prover is the maker's:
an equation between two terms; who lays G pays it. TESTS WITH CODE ON THE BOOK
(named Bool premises): hT (`tiesB`) · hbk (`bookCutsU`). Payers lie, at whatever book the
library's maker of books returns: `hT_head_U` (AtFullSide/K12/TiesAtHeadU.lean), `bookCutsU_head`
(AtFullSide/K12/CutsAtHead.lean); not called here. A CLAUSE ON VALUES: hleft (`LeftAtStandU`.rowsSay
: `SaysAt`). Beside it, not called. (a) AtFullSide/K12/OnFreeTAtHeadUPaid.lean's `onFreeT_head_U_paid` ends
in the whole condition under both ties, so it pays the END at the return past hleft; it asks hα (the
parts' key is the instance's), hst (the prover's stored table is the committer's), hgS (the eighth
sub-protocol's half), hB (the book is the library's) and hAns (each answer of the instance's key is
its row's own): none of the five names a coin k that the book lends, a challenge, a stand or a
carried block; hst and hAns read the index and the committer's randomness, hAns the key besides:
AtFullSide/K12/OnAtRunUPaid.lean goes that road. (b) the acceptance side's `saysAt_U`
(K12/AtFile/SaysAtU.lean:82; not called): `SaysAt` at any
job, input, front and coins C, from: the state on entry reads a state s's statement and group · s is
in order, no open row marked as a sample row, the group's row count, the group's members · what the
shared thread's open items say at border 9 · the words' tie at C. ITS HEAD BEARS "NOT IN FRONT OF A
LAW OVER COINS: the thread's stand is a premise": whoever calls it here and keeps its letters takes
that label, and owes the step from the border's state to the stand. Either payer needs hα.

What the proof pays at every stand: le, leS, heardFit, heard, fold (`five_at_run`), door
(`door_clause_any`), asks from heardFit and `SaysAt` (`asks_heard`): these seven through
`onFreeT_head_U` (OnFreeTAtHeadU.lean), its premises on the place, the cut and the challenges by
AtProof/SideAtU.lean's four laws, the place's facts and hρ · trees (`trees_head_U_pub`,
TreesAtHeadUPub.lean). At the first member On asks nothing.

WHAT On SAYS, FOR WHOEVER HOLDS IT AGAINST A MEASURE. On is the library's `OnFreeT`, eight clauses,
not this file's. le, leS, heardFit, heard speak of the stand and the front alone. door, fold and
trees are equations between what the job makes of the stand's input and the carried coins, and what
the front lists. asks: under the head it follows from heardFit and `SaysAt` (one direction alone is
shown). `SaysAt`, to its text: for the group under test in the state on entry, each row r that the
test takes in has "value ρ S r m = ρ.val r.target" (Johnson/Desc/Means/Says.lean): the rows are
those of the job's state on entry, which door sets equal to the simulators' function of the key and
the front; the words m are made of the index's reader, the table's randomness and the carried coins.
So door with asks says: THE AFFINE ROWS THAT THE FRONT FIXES ARE TRUE OF THE HIDDEN WORDS. It names
no subset of its own: it is harmless if and only if hleft is a theorem at all coins: every input of
the relation, every k, every due list of challenges, each called part. THIS FILE DOES NOT SHOW THAT.

THE FALL-BACK (`doorUF`, DoorsByShape.lean: where the fold over the eight blocks in front fails, or
the seat's way in refuses, the state on entry is `fallU`, a term of the plan's shape). `onFreeT`
LETS THE FALL-BACK STATE THROUGH, BY LAWS: `door_clause_any` has the clause door "whether or not the
fold in front returns" (both sides are one function, `doorUF` | `simDoorU`, of the key, which is the
input's public part, and of the rounds seen and the stored columns opened at "LOC"'s positions,
which the front lists); `five_at_run` and `trees_head_U_pub` ask nothing of the fold; `saysAt_fails`
(SaysAtFall.lean) has `SaysAt` there for nothing. So `onAtRun_U` gives On at every called stand, the
fall-back's among them (`leftAtStandU_where_the_fold_fails` has the first way into it, the fold's
failure; the second, the seat's refusal, falls under `saysAt_fallU` and has no corollary here),
`good_testOnU`'s exact is claimed there too, job and simulators falling back alike, and NO PREMISE
OF THESE STATEMENTS CARRIES "THE FALL-BACK IS NOT TAKEN". That it is never taken at a called part is
a law of its own: `atHandAtU_at_run'` (AtProof/HalfAtPure.lean:179), under hα and hst; not called
here. Toward EARLIER senders On does shut states out, through asks [a reasoning, no law]:
if a sender in front pads or sends a default, a row can be false of the words, and `SaysAt` fails.

Through its imports this file stands over files under Johnson/Goal/ (a walk of the import lines).





Limits. The rule moves the debt and pays none of it. The condition reads the input and the carried
values: no later law may take it as a hypothesis on a run and then speak of the random values as
sampled anew. The simulators' job is given the stored table's columns opened at "LOC"'s positions,
which are made from the weights. Of the walk (runC), not of play. Rows stay at the wide filling's
types: no crossing to the online prover is typed here. `first_ties_at_shared_test` is the middle of
the proof of `five_at_test₂` (Sim2/SharedChainAtRun.lean) cut out as a statement,
because that law ends in `FiveAt` and does not hand out what `onFreeT_head_U` asks. The full size
alone, and the format's second hash function alone. Nothing on completeness, soundness or hiding.
No property is claimed.
-/
